NullPointerException explained

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = null;
        System.out.println(s.length());
    }
}
```

Error:
```
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "String.length()" because "<local1>" is null
	at Main.main(Main.java:4)
```

`s` holds `null`, meaning no object, so calling `.length()` on it throws. Check for null first, or make sure the value is assigned before use.

Corrected version:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = null;
        System.out.println(s == null ? 0 : s.length());
    }
}
```

